# What the work taught us

These are lessons from recorded cases, not a controlled benchmark of AI philosophy. Each links an observation to a practical implication and a remaining uncertainty.

## Separate contexts do not guarantee different ideas

The first ten authors worked separately, yet their themes converged around rights, institutions, evidence, and revisability. Later batches allocated broad fields and tried other starting methods. Context separation helped keep inputs distinct; it did not establish intellectual diversity. [Generation history](generation.md).

## A large panel can still fail to discriminate

None of the midterm's 2,400 primary reviews recommended setting an essay aside. High scores therefore did not supply a shortlist. The coordinator had to compare actual objections, contributions, and unresolved problems; later tests examined the reviewers themselves. Those diagnostics covered specific fixtures, not general philosophical competence. [Midterm and diagnostics](evaluation.md).

## Criticism can change who gets another chance

A fresh critic found that E079's achieved result had been compared with E036's possible future improvement. E079 returned to the candidate set. The lesson is to compare what texts currently establish and record when a selection judgment changes. This case does not show that every rejection was independently corrected. [The decision and correction](evaluation.md#what-the-scores-missed).

## Check the contribution before paying for a full draft

Three completed manuscripts failed the creative series' contribution check. From attempt four, an independent critic examined the proposal first; four later attempts stopped before drafting. This made a concrete change to the workflow. It does not establish how much compute was saved or that every early rejection was right. [Creative-series record](generation.md#check-the-contribution-before-writing-the-essay).

## Shorter can mean different

While shortening the earlier Claude pilot, an editor removed a qualification that limited its claim. A fresh critic caught the change; the qualification was restored while twelve other cuts remained. Editing an argument needs a meaning check as well as a word count. [E076 and the recorded correction](../essays/E076/README.md).

## More revision was not always the chosen version

Two branching experiments compared a starting text with one-cycle and three-cycle alternatives. One selector preferred one cycle, the other three. Preserve branches and compare the actual texts. The cases do not identify an optimal revision count: models, contexts, and tasks also varied. [Branching design](generation.md#six-ways-to-begin).

## A narrower result can be more defensible

E012's later version explains why destroying promised evidence can leave a duty to help after compensation, while a control case limits that duty. E050's selected version retains an explicit result for a specified family of systems. The useful question is what survives the objections, not how broad the opening promise sounds. Narrowing alone does not establish novelty or significance. [E012](../essays/E012/README.md) · [E050](../essays/E050/README.md).

## Keep three kinds of success separate

A file can pass its integrity checks, a campaign can fill all its review slots, and an essay can still have an unresolved philosophical problem. The archive lets readers inspect the reasoning behind decisions. It does not certify originality, complete provider capture, or the absence of all indirect human influence. [Evidence](../evidence/README.md) · [Scope of the record](provenance.md).
